  "why": "The decisive call is the reading of the bullet. 'Hilbert's tenth problem for a number field' in the list's context is the Denef-Lipshitz question about rings of integers O_K (the classes Denef, Pheidas, Shapiro-Shlapentokh, Poonen etc. are all ring results, and K=Q is then Matiyasevich). On that reading Koymans-Pagano and Alpöge-Bhargava-Ho-Shnidman each answer the whole question ('all number fields'); ABHS is accepted in Inventiones (digested), Koymans-Pagano remains a preprint with only Poonen's work on a supporting theorem, so unreviewed. The OpenAI rational-field manuscript (recorded twice, as openai-hilbert-q-2026-10 and openai-math-004) addresses the field Q, a different question under the ring reading, so it is a variant; even under the field reading it would be only a case (Q alone). Variable-count improvements (Matiyasevich-Sun, Ding-Li, Sun) and the trinomial paper do not change which fields are covered and are variants. Conditional results (Mazur-Rubin, Murty-Pasten) and tools/expository/alternative proofs of supporting lemmas are none. Pre-snapshot class results are cases; Poonen 2003 and Mazur-Rubin-Shlapentokh concern subrings of Q / definability over Q and are variants.",
